schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: Tokens as Coordination Tools
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: concept
  summary: >-
    Explains how tokens function as coordination mechanisms for distributed
    groups: signaling (temperature checks before formal votes), on-chain vs
    off-chain voting, reputation-based alternatives to pure token wealth, and
    incentive/penalty design. Walks through MakerDAO, Gitcoin DAO, and
    KlimaDAO as real examples, then names the recurring failure modes (low
    participation, wealth concentration, hidden multisig hierarchies,
    short-termism) and points to the SuperBenefit anticapture framework as a
    design response.
  audience: regenerative community members and DAO organizers weighing whether/how to use tokens for governance
  known_tensions:
    - token-weighted-voting vs one-person-one-voice ideals
    - decentralization-as-stated-value vs multisig-concentrated-power-in-practice
    - short-term-price-speculation vs long-term-ecosystem-health
  related_concepts:
    - token-based-coordination-mechanisms
    - reputation-based-governance
    - anticapture-governance-design
  related_resources:
    - SuperBenefit Knowledge Garden
    - MakerDAO
    - Gitcoin DAO
    - KlimaDAO
    - Colony
    - Tally
    - Snapshot
  maturity: raw
  public_use: source-linked-unreviewed
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/tokens-coordination-tools.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  source_lineage: tokens-coordination-tools.md
  notes: |
    # assessed-but-excluded
    - "Try This" exercise (visit Snapshot, look at active proposals) folded into
      the encyclopedia entry's framing rather than a separate object; it's an
      exercise prompt, not a distinct typed fact.
    - no people/community profiles, exact locations, TEK, or funding/legal
      recommendations in this article; no high-risk trigger identified.
